<title>USA: McDonnell Douglas to produce Navy missiles.</title>
<headline>McDonnell Douglas to produce Navy missiles.</headline>
<dateline>ST. LOUIS 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>McDonnell Douglas Corp said Thursday the U.S. Navy has approved low-rate initial production of its Standoff Land Attack Missile Expanded Response (SLAM ER) weapon.</p>
<p>The company said the decision clears the way for production to begin on 60 of the missiles with fiscal 1997 funds.  The Navy plans to retrofit all of its previous series SLAM missiles to SLAM ERs, McDonnell Douglas said.</p>
<p>Financial terms were not announced.</p>
<p>McDonnell Douglas shares were up 5/8 Thursday at 62-1/4.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
</text>
